in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @peer
in @aikido
in @mirror/store
in @time
in @time/past

# @peer/redirect — Tier-2 peer response species; the crystal-chain
# walker refusing re-litigation via OID-verifiability.
#
# Species under @peer. Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara Round-3 per Alex
# Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.7.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Tier 2 of the three-tier @peer response surface (per
# `shards/aikido.mirror`): fires when the peer's own @cyberpunk/
# algedonic reading exceeds the Tier-1 threshold (Tier-1 admits no
# response) but remains below the Tier-2 threshold (Tier-3
# recognition bomb not yet warranted).
#
# The Tier-2 discipline: `redirect(crystal_oid)` walks the Crystal
# chain backwards via `@mirror/store.walk_crystal_chain(oid)` and
# refuses re-litigation because the peer's past-position on the
# question is content-addressed. The response: "We crystallized this
# on OID X, here's the receipt. If you have new substrate that
# changes the reading, present it. Otherwise, the crystallized
# reading stands."
#
# Corresponds to aikido's `tenkan` (turning — redirecting the
# momentum along the peer's own past-trajectory via @time/past).
# The peer does not counter; the peer redirects the incoming
# momentum back toward the crystallized history that already
# discharged the question.
#
# **OID-verifiability is load-bearing**: the crystal chain is
# content-addressed at @mirror/store altitude. The peer cannot
# fabricate a crystal; the walker verifies the crystal-chain
# integrity via @mirror/store.verify. If the crystal does not exist
# or the chain is malformed, redirect fails and the loop escalates
# to Tier 3.
#
# === Composition-primitive naming ===
#
# Per feedback_composition_primitive_naming_convention:
#
#   peer_redirect_of_crystal_oid(p: peer, crystal_oid: ref, target: peer)
#     -> crystal_chain_reading
#
# Input-shape: `crystal_oid` (the OID of the crystal-chain-head the
# peer redirects the target to). Output: `crystal_chain_reading` (the
# typed carrier for the walked chain + refusal-of-re-litigation
# verdict).
#
# === Composition edge with @time/past ===
#
# The crystal_oid is typically produced by @time/past.history_with
# (target) — the peer's own past-trajectory with the target. When
# the target's incoming perturbation matches a prior crystallized
# reading, @peer.redirect refuses re-litigation by pointing at the
# crystal-chain-head OID as content-addressed receipt.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/peer/redirect.mirror`** — clean naming space.
# 2. **`shards/peer.mirror`** — reviewed. Family-root; sibling species
#    at Tier-2 altitude; no conflict.
# 3. **`shards/mirror/store/crystal.mirror`** — reviewed. Crystal<T>
#    carrier this species walks; no duplication, composition.
# 4. **`shards/time/past.mirror`** — reviewed. @time/past.history_with
#    is the source of crystal_oid; composition edge declared.
# 5. **`shards/peer/reflect.mirror`** — sibling Tier-1 species this
#    tick; distinct altitude, no conflict.
#
# === The crystal_chain_reading carrier ===
#
# The typed return of `peer_redirect_of_crystal_oid`. Composes:
#
#   chain_head_oid    — the OID of the crystal-chain-head walked to
#                        (per @mirror/store OID discipline).
#   chain_length      — how many crystals in the chain (per
#                        @mirror/store.walk_crystal_chain contract).
#   re_litigation_refused — the verdict of the refusal (Pass iff the
#                        chain is well-formed and content-addressed).
#   receipt_reference — a content-addressed reference the peer offers
#                        the target as receipt (per @kintsugi/consent
#                        discipline — the target can independently
#                        verify the receipt via @mirror/store).
type crystal_chain_reading = {
  chain_head_oid:        ref,
  chain_length:          nat,
  re_litigation_refused: verdict,
  receipt_reference:     ref,
}

# === peer_redirect_of_crystal_oid — the Tier-2 dispatcher action ===
#
# Body discharges per-realisation. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
#
# Sentinel: `peer=redirect-tier-2-crystal-chain-walk-refuses-re-
# litigation`.
peer_redirect_of_crystal_oid(p: peer, crystal_oid: ref, target: peer)
  -> crystal_chain_reading
requires redirect_targets_valid_crystal(p, crystal_oid)
{ \ }

# === redirect_targets_valid_crystal — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - p is a well-formed peer
#   - crystal_oid resolves via @mirror/store.exists to a valid
#     Crystal<T> object
#   - the crystal-chain from crystal_oid is walkable via
#     @mirror/store.walk_crystal_chain (contract: returns finite
#     chain OR malformed-chain error)
#   - the peer's own @cyberpunk/algedonic reading is ABOVE Tier-1
#     threshold and BELOW Tier-2 threshold (Tier-2 domain)
#   - the target's crystal-chain-membership can be verified (the
#     target is a peer in the crystal-chain's participation set per
#     @mirror/store.crystal_participants)
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (OID resolvability,
# walk_crystal_chain discharge which is itself Rice-safe, algedonic-
# magnitude comparison, participant-set membership check).
#
# Sentinel: `peer=redirect-targets-valid-crystal`.
bilateral redirect_targets_valid_crystal {
  sentinel "peer=redirect-targets-valid-crystal"
  arity 2
}
redirect_targets_valid_crystal(p: peer, crystal_oid: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Recognition candidates surfaced (DO NOT RATIFY at this landing)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# #R-oid-verifiability-refuses-re-litigation-by-construction — the
# crystal chain is content-addressed; the receipt cannot be
# fabricated; the target can independently verify. First-witness
# this tick. Second-witness gate opens on empirical firing at
# Reed's pillar surface. Held at CANDIDATE strength.
#
# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# - peer_redirect_witnessing bilateral composing redirect_targets_
#   valid_crystal + walk_crystal_chain discharge
# - .redirect cli-boundary wrapper at @mirror/peer altitude

out @peer/redirect
out crystal_chain_reading
out peer_redirect_of_crystal_oid
out redirect_targets_valid_crystal
